<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baltic Fleet</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Baltic Fleet is the branch of the Russian navy based on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baltic-sea">Baltic Sea</a>. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-japanese-war">Russo-Japanese War</a> much of it was sent around the world as the Second Pacific Squadron. Its destruction by the Japanese at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tsushima">Battle of Tsushima</a> in 1905 was a humiliating defeat that weakened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> and contributed to the revolution of 1905.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baltic-fleet.jpg" alt="Baltic Fleet" width="315" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Russian Navy Tatiana Saidbaeva · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Great_emblem_of_the_Baltic_fleet.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
